<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    Templated from VFEP's VFEP_WarcasketShoulders_Siegebreaker (VFEP commit e237aba,
    1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Misc/Apparel_Various.xml); fields not discussed here are Siegebreaker's.
    Tags, blunt plating and the Odyssey GravlitePanel split follow the armor's header.

    Tuning: Plasteel 70 (Siegebreaker 60) is the 10th-gen shoulder-to-armor ratio, roughly 0.4
    (Siegebreaker 60/145, Guardian 80/200, Controller 60/150, Sarcophagus 60/145, Brute
    60/160), applied to the armor's 180 and rounded to VFEP's 10-plasteel steps. No spacer
    components, like the Siegebreaker, Guardian and Sarcophagus shoulders.

    Abilities, the breaching arms:
    - SCWC_BreachPower +0.5: landings deal 900 to a wall cell instead of 600, enough for
      plasteel and uranium walls; structures only (StatDefs/BreachPower.xml).
    - MeleeHitChance and MeleeDodgeChance x1.15 through the ApparelExtension: a step under
      Shock's x1.2 shoulders, the only VFEP precedent for the pair, because this set also
      carries 10th-gen plating and a shield where Shock has neither.
    - No jump range; the range lives on the armor. No EnergyShieldRechargeRate offset
      (Siegebreaker's +1): VEF's CompShieldBubble reads that stat off the apparel, not the
      pawn, so the offset never reaches the shield.

    Compat: SOS2Patch.xml and the VGE vacuum patch leave shoulder pads alone, as VFEP's and
    VGE1's own patches do for VFEP's. The 1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/ root rescales the
    plating and adds bulk, as CE's does for VFEP's.

    Draw order: a worn apparel node's altitude is its drawData offset y (added verbatim by
    PawnRenderTree.TryGetMatrix) plus PawnRenderUtility.AltitudeForLayer(layer), 0.000366 per
    layer unit, the layer being the parent's base (ApparelBody 20, ApparelHead 70) plus the
    piece's index among that parent's apparel; the y offsets on VFEP's bases are what order the
    pieces. Only this piece moves, so every helmet and armor, ours or VFEP's, keeps its VFEP
    altitude and foundry mix-and-match stays consistent.
    - North 0.05 (base 0.2, which puts pauldrons over the shell at 0.107): the art wants the
      shell's back frame over the pauldron edges, so about 0.058, still above the bodysuit
      (VFEP_Warcasket_Bodysuit, drawn through vanilla ProcessApparel with null drawData, near
      0.008 in every facing), the helmet (0.026) and pack-layer apparel (layer 93, 0.034).
    - South 0.014 (base 0.02, which lands at 0.027 to 0.028, just over the helmets' 0.027):
      the art wants the helmet over the pauldron edges, so 0.021 to 0.022, at least 0.004 under
      any helmet and 0.003 over the shell (0.017 to 0.018), above post-apparel wounds (layer
      30, 0.011) and firefoam (40, 0.015). Hair and beard (about 0.022) can draw over them on a
      bare head, as hair does over shoulders anyway.
    East/west inherit the base's 0.02: XmlInheritance merges same-named elements recursively,
    so only the changed facings are listed.
  -->
  <VFEPirates.WarcasketDef ParentName="VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase">
    <defName>SCWC_WarcasketShoulders_Shipcracker</defName>
    <label>shipcracker warcasket shoulders</label>
    <shortDescription>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with improved impact dispersion, equipped with melee assistor modules and hardened breaching arms that let a landing tear through plasteel.</shortDescription>
    <description>Specialized spacer-tech warcasket pauldrons with improved impact dispersion, equipped with melee assistor modules and hardened breaching arms that let a landing tear through plasteel.\n\nAn Imperial pattern, not a pirate one: boarding corps built it on the 10th-generation spacer chassis to cross the gap between two ships and open the far hull from the outside. Salvage and desertion have since put it in foundries far from any Imperial dock.\n\nA shipcracker launches through the vacuum, lands on the enemy hull, punches through to the interior and takes the ship room by room. Under gravity the same burn clears a wall or a roof in a single hop. The shield stops bullets, not blades: pilots are chosen for a taste for close work.</description>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders</texPath>
    </graphicData>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>20</Mass>
      <ArmorRating_Sharp>2</ArmorRating_Sharp>
      <ArmorRating_Blunt>1.5</ArmorRating_Blunt>
      <ArmorRating_Heat>1</ArmorRating_Heat>
      <Insulation_Cold>22</Insulation_Cold>
      <Insulation_Heat>22</Insulation_Heat>
      <EquipDelay>1</EquipDelay>
    </statBases>
    <equippedStatOffsets>
      <SlaveSuppressionOffset MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Ideology">0.2</SlaveSuppressionOffset>
      <VacuumResistance MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.1</VacuumResistance>
      <SCWC_BreachPower>0.5</SCWC_BreachPower>
    </equippedStatOffsets>
    <costList>
      <Plasteel>70</Plasteel>
      <GravlitePanel MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">10</GravlitePanel>
    </costList>
    <researchPrerequisites>
      <li>VFEP_SpacerWarcaskets</li>
    </researchPrerequisites>
    <apparel>
      <bodyPartGroups>
        <li>Shoulders</li>
        <li>Arms</li>
        <li>Hands</li>
        <li>Neck</li>
      </bodyPartGroups>
      <wornGraphicPath>Things/Pawn/Warcasketlike/WarcasketShipcracker/WarcasketShipcrackerShoulders</wornGraphicPath>
      <!-- Under the shell facing north and under the helmet facing south; see
           "Draw order" in the header. -->
      <drawData>
        <dataNorth><offset>(0, 0.05, 0)</offset></dataNorth>
        <dataSouth><offset>(0, 0.014, 0)</offset></dataSouth>
      </drawData>
      <layers>
        <li>OnSkin</li>
        <li>Middle</li>
        <li>Shell</li>
      </layers>
      <tags>
        <li>WarcasketVeteran</li>
        <li>WarcasketAll</li>
      </tags>
    </apparel>
    <modExtensions>
      <li Class="VEF.Apparels.ApparelExtension">
        <!-- priority: makes this entry the survivor when VEF merges it with the one
             VFEP_WarcasketShoulderPadBase carries; see the armor def's header. -->
        <priority>1</priority>
        <equippedStatFactors>
          <MeleeHitChance>1.15</MeleeHitChance>
          <MeleeDodgeChance>1.15</MeleeDodgeChance>
        </equippedStatFactors>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
  </VFEPirates.WarcasketDef>
</Defs>
